{
  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a persistent upward bias when recent history shows volatility followed by a spike; true outcomes frequently reverse direction within the first 5 days of the forecast horizon.",
    "When sentiment is near zero (0.00) despite rising price trends, the model overestimates momentum and fails to account for mean reversion spikes seen in the second half of the 30-day window.",
    "The model ignores short-term volatility clustering; true outcomes show sharp drops (e.g., from ~64 to ~59) that the linear extrapolation completely misses.",
    "Forecast accuracy degrades significantly when the last 3 days of history contain a high sentiment score (0.20 or higher), as the model assumes continued growth while actual data shows immediate reversal.",
    "Apply a downward correction factor of approximately 4-6% to the first 10 days of the forecast if the historical trend is upward but sentiment remains neutral."
  ]
}
